WEBVTT

00:00:01.286 --> 00:00:18.721
The Place was a small town in Massachusetts, North America.

00:00:18.781 --> 00:00:36.558
It was a cold evening in December 1862.

00:00:36.618 --> 00:00:40.051
Snow was falling softly.

00:00:40.111 --> 00:00:47.026
In the living room of a small house, four sisters were sitting by the fire.

00:00:47.085 --> 00:00:54.791
Their names were Meg, Joe, Beth, and Amy March.

00:00:54.851 --> 00:00:58.434
Meg was 16 years old.

00:00:58.494 --> 00:01:00.794
Joe was 15.

00:01:00.854 --> 00:01:07.467
Beth was 13 years old and Amy was 12.

00:01:07.527 --> 00:01:12.812
Their mother, Mrs. March, was not in the house.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:17.244
She was visiting a poor, sick family.

00:01:17.304 --> 00:01:23.128
Their father, Mr. March, was far away from home.

00:01:23.188 --> 00:01:25.330
It was wartime.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:30.465
Mr. March was working in a hospital for soldiers.

00:01:30.525 --> 00:01:34.968
The four sisters were knitting with wool.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:38.670
They were knitting socks for the soldiers.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.693
They worked and they talked.

00:01:42.753 --> 00:01:47.966
We are poor, said Meg, the eldest girl.

00:01:48.026 --> 00:01:50.488
It is terrible.

00:01:50.548 --> 00:01:53.389
Meg was very pretty.

00:01:53.449 --> 00:01:57.914
She had large eyes and soft brown hair.

00:01:57.974 --> 00:02:05.242
Other girls have lots of pretty things, said Amy, the youngest girl.

00:02:05.302 --> 00:02:10.055
Amy had golden hair and blue eyes.

00:02:10.114 --> 00:02:15.998
I hate girls' work and girls' things, said Joe.

00:02:16.058 --> 00:02:18.750
She was tall and thin.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.582
She had beautiful long red hair.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:26.930
I don't want to stay at home, she said.

00:02:26.990 --> 00:02:30.459
I want to fight in the war!"

00:02:30.518 --> 00:02:33.530
Then Beth spoke.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:39.842
Yes, we are poor, she said, but we are lucky too.

00:02:39.902 --> 00:02:45.965
We have father and mother, and we have each other.

00:02:46.024 --> 00:02:49.676
Beth was very shy.

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:56.197
She was afraid of strangers, but she loved her family very much.

00:02:56.257 --> 00:03:05.108
Yes, we have each other," said Joe, and the girls were happy again.

00:03:05.168 --> 00:03:10.319
It's six o'clock, said Meg.

00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:12.890
Be quick, everybody.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.000
Mother is coming.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.270
We must get supper ready.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:22.192
Joe brought more wood for the fire.

00:03:22.252 --> 00:03:24.571
Meg lit the lamps.

00:03:24.631 --> 00:03:28.793
Beth and Amy put the food on the table.

00:03:28.853 --> 00:03:34.136
The door opened and Mrs. March came into the room.

00:03:34.196 --> 00:03:40.942
Mrs. March was not beautiful, but she was very kind and good.

00:03:41.002 --> 00:03:44.634
Her daughters had a special name for her.

00:03:44.694 --> 00:03:47.806
They called her Marmee.

00:03:47.866 --> 00:03:50.749
How are you, my dears?

00:03:50.809 --> 00:03:52.610
Said Mrs. March.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:55.098
Did you have a good day?

00:03:55.158 --> 00:04:00.386
Yes, thank you, Marmy," replied the Four Sisters.

00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:06.130
Come, sit down by the fire, Marmy, said Meg.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:09.253
Supper is ready.

00:04:09.313 --> 00:04:18.721
After Supper, Mrs. March said, girls, I have a wonderful surprise.

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:21.695
Everybody was excited.

00:04:21.755 --> 00:04:24.330
Is it a letter from father?"

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.752
asked Joe.

00:04:25.812 --> 00:04:29.114
Yes, replied Mrs. March.

00:04:29.174 --> 00:04:33.748
Father has a Christmas message for all of you.

00:04:33.808 --> 00:04:38.202
The girls read their father's letter.

00:04:38.262 --> 00:04:49.958
To my four little women, the letter said, my dears, I will not see you again for a long time.

00:04:50.018 --> 00:04:54.038
I think of you all every day.

00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:56.820
Take care of your mother.

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.253
Be good and work hard.

00:05:00.313 --> 00:05:12.591
Happy Christmas from your loving father.

00:05:12.651 --> 00:05:31.754
Chapter 2 A Wonderful Christmas A few days later it was Christmas Day.

00:05:31.814 --> 00:05:36.058
On Christmas morning the girls woke early.

00:05:36.118 --> 00:05:41.642
Each girl had one present, a book from their mother.

00:05:41.702 --> 00:05:44.134
They ran downstairs.

00:05:44.194 --> 00:05:46.726
They wanted to thank her.

00:05:46.786 --> 00:05:50.432
But Mrs. March was not there.

00:05:50.492 --> 00:05:54.829
A special Christmas breakfast was on the table.

00:05:54.889 --> 00:05:59.992
There was lots of food, and everybody was hungry.

00:06:00.052 --> 00:06:03.584
But the girls waited for their mother.

00:06:03.644 --> 00:06:06.686
They waited nearly an hour.

00:06:06.746 --> 00:06:10.338
At last, their mother came home.

00:06:10.398 --> 00:06:13.050
Merry Christmas, Marmy!

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:18.954
The girls shouted, come, sit down, let's eat breakfast.

00:06:19.013 --> 00:06:24.186
Mary Christmas little daughters, said Mrs. March.

00:06:24.246 --> 00:06:28.908
Listen, I have something to tell you.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:33.130
There is a poor woman, Mrs. Hummel.

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:35.321
She lives in the town.

00:06:35.381 --> 00:06:37.972
She has seven children.

00:06:38.032 --> 00:06:39.974
One is a baby.

00:06:40.034 --> 00:06:45.636
The Hummel's house is very cold, and they have no food.

00:06:45.696 --> 00:06:48.957
Will you give them a Christmas present?

00:06:49.017 --> 00:06:52.608
Will you give them your breakfast?"

00:06:52.668 --> 00:06:56.311
All the girls were very hungry.

00:06:56.371 --> 00:06:59.482
For a moment, nobody spoke.

00:06:59.542 --> 00:07:04.396
Then Joe said, yes, we will, Marmy.

00:07:04.456 --> 00:07:07.858
Let's take the food to them now.

00:07:07.918 --> 00:07:12.560
It was early morning, and it was cold.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.108
The girls walked quickly through the snow.

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:22.060
They carried baskets of food and wood for the fire.

00:07:22.119 --> 00:07:28.254
The Hummel family lived in one small room.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:32.136
The room was in a house near a river.

00:07:32.196 --> 00:07:37.150
The windows of the room were broken and there was no fire.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:40.112
Mrs. Hummel lay in her bed.

00:07:40.172 --> 00:07:41.968
She was ill.

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:48.046
The baby was crying, and the children were cold and hungry.

00:07:48.106 --> 00:07:53.759
The humble children saw the March sisters and the baskets of food.

00:07:53.819 --> 00:07:56.230
They shouted happily.

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.652
Thank you!

00:07:57.712 --> 00:07:58.852
Thank you!

00:07:58.912 --> 00:08:00.684
They shouted.

00:08:00.744 --> 00:08:05.876
The girls made a fire, and they put the food on the table.

00:08:05.936 --> 00:08:09.028
Mrs. March made some tea.

00:08:09.088 --> 00:08:12.008
Soon the room was warm.

00:08:12.068 --> 00:08:17.530
The hungry children ate the food and they laughed.

00:08:17.590 --> 00:08:22.454
Later, Mrs. March and her daughters went home.

00:08:22.513 --> 00:08:29.268
They had bread and milk for breakfast, but they were very happy.

00:08:29.328 --> 00:08:33.722
The March sisters often acted in plays.

00:08:33.782 --> 00:08:36.314
Joe wrote the plays.

00:08:36.374 --> 00:08:41.347
The girls acted in a small room at the top of the house.

00:08:41.407 --> 00:08:47.350
They put on brightly colored clothes and they enjoyed themselves.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:52.413
On Christmas evening, the girls acted in a play.

00:08:52.473 --> 00:08:55.034
All their friends came.

00:08:55.094 --> 00:08:58.746
Everybody enjoyed the play.

00:08:58.806 --> 00:09:05.180
Later, their friends went home and the girls had a lovely surprise.

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:08.142
Mrs. March called to them.

00:09:08.202 --> 00:09:11.647
Supper is ready, she said.

00:09:11.707 --> 00:09:14.751
The girls ran downstairs.

00:09:14.811 --> 00:09:19.223
They saw lots of delicious food on the table.

00:09:19.283 --> 00:09:24.355
Cakes, sweets, fruit, and ice cream.

00:09:24.415 --> 00:09:28.106
Where did this lovely food come from, Marme?

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:29.818
Amy asked.

00:09:29.877 --> 00:09:32.288
Mrs. March smiled.

00:09:32.348 --> 00:09:36.872
Old Mr. Lawrence sent it, she replied.

00:09:36.932 --> 00:09:41.666
Old Mr. Lawrence, our neighbor, asked Meg.

00:09:41.726 --> 00:09:43.788
She was surprised.

00:09:43.848 --> 00:09:47.720
But we don't know him, she said.

00:09:47.780 --> 00:09:52.613
He heard about your breakfast, said Mrs. March.

00:09:52.673 --> 00:09:56.426
He has sent you a special Christmas supper.

00:09:56.486 --> 00:09:59.538
The girls looked at each other.

00:09:59.598 --> 00:10:11.553
This is a wonderful Christmas, Beth said.

00:10:11.613 --> 00:10:29.662
Chapter 3 Lori Next to the March's small house, there was a large house.

00:10:29.722 --> 00:10:34.634
The sisters called this house the Lawrence House.

00:10:34.694 --> 00:10:39.088
It belonged to their neighbor, Mr. Lawrence.

00:10:39.148 --> 00:10:44.360
Mr. Lawrence was old and he was very rich.

00:10:44.421 --> 00:10:47.834
His house was very beautiful.

00:10:47.894 --> 00:10:51.726
He lived in the house with his grandson.

00:10:51.786 --> 00:10:57.919
His grandson was 15, the same age as Joe.

00:10:57.979 --> 00:11:08.803
Sometimes the March sisters saw Mr. Lawrence's grandson, but the boy was always alone.

00:11:08.863 --> 00:11:15.226
A few days after Christmas, Joe was in her garden.

00:11:15.286 --> 00:11:19.286
She was wearing boots and an old coat.

00:11:19.346 --> 00:11:21.696
Joe was busy.

00:11:21.756 --> 00:11:27.188
She was sweeping snow from the path with a broom.

00:11:27.248 --> 00:11:31.840
Joe looked up at the Lawrence house.

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:35.740
She saw a face looking out of a window.

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:39.502
It was Mr. Lawrence's grandson.

00:11:39.562 --> 00:11:42.282
The boy is sad.

00:11:42.342 --> 00:11:45.900
He is lonely, thought Joe.

00:11:45.959 --> 00:11:48.928
Then she had an idea.

00:11:48.988 --> 00:11:53.190
She took some snow, and she made a ball with it.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.362
She threw the ball at the window.

00:11:56.422 --> 00:12:00.494
The boy laughed, and he opened the window.

00:12:00.555 --> 00:12:01.835
Hello?

00:12:01.895 --> 00:12:03.396
Called Joe.

00:12:03.456 --> 00:12:05.428
Are you ill?

00:12:05.488 --> 00:12:09.500
I was ill last week, said the boy.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:13.482
I'm better now, but I'm very bored.

00:12:13.542 --> 00:12:16.324
I am not doing anything.

00:12:16.384 --> 00:12:19.566
I'll visit you, said Joe.

00:12:19.626 --> 00:12:24.458
Yes, please come, said the boy.

00:12:24.518 --> 00:12:30.830
A few minutes later, Joe knocked on the door of the Lawrence house.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:34.440
She was carrying a small basket.

00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:38.872
The basket was full of apples and cakes.

00:12:38.932 --> 00:12:45.602
The boy opened the door, and Joe gave him the basket.

00:12:45.662 --> 00:12:49.302
These things are for you," she said.

00:12:49.363 --> 00:12:51.715
They are from my mother.

00:12:51.775 --> 00:12:55.628
Thank you very much, said the boy.

00:12:55.688 --> 00:12:57.720
Please come in.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.352
My name is Laurie.

00:13:00.412 --> 00:13:03.366
And you're Joe, aren't you?

00:13:03.426 --> 00:13:06.118
Yes, said Joe.

00:13:06.178 --> 00:13:08.901
She was very surprised.

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:11.812
How do you know my name?

00:13:11.872 --> 00:13:15.664
I know your name," said Laurie.

00:13:15.724 --> 00:13:18.826
I know all your sister's names.

00:13:18.886 --> 00:13:22.798
You call to each other in your garden.

00:13:22.858 --> 00:13:29.373
Sometimes I see you with your mother, Laurie said sadly.

00:13:29.432 --> 00:13:32.074
I have no mother.

00:13:32.134 --> 00:13:38.108
My parents are dead, so I live here with my grandfather.

00:13:38.168 --> 00:13:42.773
But my grandfather is not at home today.

00:13:42.833 --> 00:13:49.968
Laurie is rich, but he's very lonely, thought Joe.

00:13:50.028 --> 00:13:57.092
I am poor, but I have a family, and I have a happy home.

00:13:57.152 --> 00:14:00.755
Please visit us, said Joe.

00:14:00.815 --> 00:14:02.636
We are neighbors.

00:14:02.696 --> 00:14:05.968
Let's be friends too.

00:14:06.028 --> 00:14:11.172
Joe and Laurie talked all afternoon.

00:14:11.232 --> 00:14:14.384
Joe talked about her family.

00:14:14.445 --> 00:14:17.558
Laurie talked about his life.

00:14:17.618 --> 00:14:20.230
He did not go to school.

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:25.453
A teacher, Mr. Brooke, came to the house every day.

00:14:25.513 --> 00:14:29.486
Mr. Brooke taught Laurie his lessons.

00:14:29.546 --> 00:14:33.488
Come into our library, said Laurie.

00:14:33.548 --> 00:14:37.931
We have many fine books in the library.

00:14:37.991 --> 00:14:43.420
The library was a beautiful room with big windows.

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:47.595
There were hundreds of interesting books on the shelves.

00:14:47.655 --> 00:14:51.636
There were many fine pictures on the walls.

00:14:51.696 --> 00:14:56.468
What a wonderful room, said Joe.

00:14:56.528 --> 00:15:00.759
Suddenly, Lori and Joe heard a noise.

00:15:00.819 --> 00:15:03.360
Grandfather has come home.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:06.790
Said Lori, I must go to him.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:09.441
Please stay here.

00:15:09.501 --> 00:15:12.986
Lori went out of the library.

00:15:13.046 --> 00:15:15.832
Joe stood by the fire.

00:15:15.892 --> 00:15:20.474
There was a picture of old Mr. Lawrence on the wall.

00:15:20.534 --> 00:15:23.526
Joe looked at the picture.

00:15:23.586 --> 00:15:29.609
The door of the library opened, but she did not turn round.

00:15:29.669 --> 00:15:37.894
Lori, she said, Mr. Lawrence, your grandfather, is not handsome.

00:15:37.954 --> 00:15:40.586
But he has a kind face.

00:15:40.646 --> 00:15:42.455
I like him.

00:15:42.515 --> 00:15:45.866
Thank you," said a voice.

00:15:45.926 --> 00:15:48.497
Joe turned round quickly.

00:15:48.557 --> 00:15:52.190
Mr. Lawrence was standing near the door.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:56.111
Oh, she said, I'm sorry.

00:15:56.131 --> 00:16:00.544
So, I'm not handsome.

00:16:00.604 --> 00:16:02.766
Asked Mr. Lawrence.

00:16:02.826 --> 00:16:06.118
Well, no sir.

00:16:06.178 --> 00:16:09.554
But I have a kind face.

00:16:09.614 --> 00:16:13.672
Yes, you do, sir," replied Joe.

00:16:13.732 --> 00:16:16.264
Mr. Lawrence laughed.

00:16:16.324 --> 00:16:18.906
I knew your grandfather.

00:16:18.966 --> 00:16:22.460
He said he was a good man.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:26.412
Now have some tea.

00:16:26.472 --> 00:16:29.886
Laurie was very happy.

00:16:29.946 --> 00:16:33.770
Laurie and Joe drank tea and they talked.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.384
Mr. Lawrence watched them.

00:16:36.444 --> 00:16:39.289
My grandson is happy.

00:16:39.349 --> 00:16:40.640
He thought.

00:16:40.700 --> 00:16:42.802
He was lonely.

00:16:42.862 --> 00:16:47.016
He must have some friends.

00:16:47.076 --> 00:16:51.148
Later, Jo went home.

00:16:51.208 --> 00:16:56.363
She told her mother and her sisters about the Lawrence's beautiful house.

00:16:56.423 --> 00:16:59.976
Marmy, please let Laurie visit us.

00:17:00.036 --> 00:17:04.984
She said, yes, dear, replied Mrs. March.

00:17:05.044 --> 00:17:09.669
Your new friend Laurie will be welcome in our house.

00:17:09.729 --> 00:17:36.244
Chapter 4 A Present for Beth Lori and the March sisters became good friends.

00:17:36.304 --> 00:17:38.946
They visited each other often.

00:17:39.006 --> 00:17:42.828
They had many happy days together.

00:17:42.888 --> 00:17:47.220
Everybody liked Lori and his grandfather.

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:52.493
Meg, Joe and Amy all went to the Lawrence house.

00:17:52.553 --> 00:17:56.245
Meg loved flowers and gardens.

00:17:56.305 --> 00:18:00.560
She liked the garden at the Lawrence house very much.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:04.465
It was winter, and there were no flowers.

00:18:04.525 --> 00:18:07.126
But there was snow on the trees.

00:18:07.186 --> 00:18:10.188
They were very beautiful.

00:18:10.248 --> 00:18:16.432
Joe wrote plays and stories, and she loved books.

00:18:16.492 --> 00:18:20.284
She liked the library at the Lawrence House.

00:18:20.344 --> 00:18:23.466
Amy liked the library, too.

00:18:23.526 --> 00:18:26.047
She painted pictures.

00:18:26.107 --> 00:18:30.178
She liked the paintings on the library walls.

00:18:30.238 --> 00:18:34.678
But Beth did not visit the Lawrence house.

00:18:34.738 --> 00:18:37.060
She was very shy.

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:40.942
She was afraid of old Mr. Lawrence.

00:18:41.002 --> 00:18:44.294
Beth did not go to school.

00:18:44.354 --> 00:18:47.174
She learned her lessons at home.

00:18:47.234 --> 00:18:52.408
Beth's life was quiet, but she was very happy.

00:18:52.468 --> 00:18:55.489
She helped her mother with the housework.

00:18:55.549 --> 00:18:58.920
She learned her lessons every day.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:19:02.272
Beth loved music.

00:19:02.332 --> 00:19:07.206
The marches had a piano, but it was very old.

00:19:07.266 --> 00:19:14.202
Beth tried to play the piano, but the music did not sound very good.

00:19:14.262 --> 00:19:18.856
One day Mr. Lawrence spoke to Mrs. March.

00:19:18.916 --> 00:19:22.360
Do your daughters play the piano?

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.770
He asked.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:28.360
Beth plays the piano, Mrs. March replied.

00:19:28.420 --> 00:19:33.299
I have a beautiful piano, said Mr. Lawrence.

00:19:33.359 --> 00:19:36.160
But nobody plays it now.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:39.302
Will Beth come to my house?

00:19:39.362 --> 00:19:42.154
Will she play the piano?

00:19:42.214 --> 00:19:46.966
Beth is very shy, Mrs. March said.

00:19:47.026 --> 00:19:52.918
Laurie and I are often out of the house, said Mr. Lawrence.

00:19:52.978 --> 00:19:55.380
Beth must come then.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:59.043
We will not hear her playing the piano.

00:19:59.103 --> 00:20:02.866
Mrs. March told Beth the news.

00:20:02.926 --> 00:20:06.380
Beth was very happy and excited.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:10.812
She wanted to play Mr. Lawrence's piano.

00:20:10.872 --> 00:20:15.905
The next day, Beth went to the Lawrence house.

00:20:15.966 --> 00:20:19.317
The house was very quiet.

00:20:19.378 --> 00:20:22.230
Good, thought Beth.

00:20:22.289 --> 00:20:25.642
Everybody is out of the house.

00:20:25.702 --> 00:20:28.794
The piano is in the living room.

00:20:28.854 --> 00:20:32.346
Beth walked very quietly into the room.

00:20:32.406 --> 00:20:35.127
She touched the piano.

00:20:35.187 --> 00:20:40.769
How beautiful it is, she thought.

00:20:40.829 --> 00:20:46.521
Some pages of music were lying on top of the piano.

00:20:46.581 --> 00:20:49.062
Beth looked at the pages.

00:20:49.122 --> 00:20:57.078
The music was not difficult, so she started to play.

00:20:57.138 --> 00:21:03.323
Beth played the piano for many hours.

00:21:03.383 --> 00:21:07.123
She enjoyed herself very much.

00:21:07.183 --> 00:21:12.054
After that, she went to the Lawrence house every day.

00:21:12.114 --> 00:21:15.935
Sometimes, Mr. Lawrence was in the house.

00:21:15.995 --> 00:21:23.976
He often listened to the music, but Beth never saw him.

00:21:24.036 --> 00:21:32.654
A few weeks passed, One day, Beth spoke to her mother.

00:21:32.714 --> 00:21:38.826
Marmy, she said, I want to thank Mr. Lawrence.

00:21:38.886 --> 00:21:41.606
He has been very kind.

00:21:41.666 --> 00:21:44.227
I will give him a present.

00:21:44.287 --> 00:21:47.778
Shall I knit a pair of slippers for him?

00:21:47.838 --> 00:21:51.699
Yes, Beth, replied Mrs. March.

00:21:51.759 --> 00:21:55.265
That's a very good idea.

00:21:55.325 --> 00:22:01.382
Beth bought some wool, and she made a beautiful pair of slippers.

00:22:01.442 --> 00:22:04.254
She took them to the Lawrence house.

00:22:04.314 --> 00:22:10.587
Mr. Lawrence was away from home, so Beth wrote a short note.

00:22:10.647 --> 00:22:14.799
She put the note and the slippers on a table.

00:22:14.860 --> 00:22:17.880
Then she went home.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:23.096
There was no reply from Mr. Lawrence that day.

00:22:23.156 --> 00:22:25.912
Oh, thought Beth.

00:22:25.972 --> 00:22:30.055
Mr. Lawrence did not like the slippers.

00:22:30.115 --> 00:22:34.278
The next morning Beth walked by the river.

00:22:34.338 --> 00:22:36.250
She was sad.

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:38.752
Later she went home.

00:22:38.812 --> 00:22:41.294
Her sisters were waiting.

00:22:41.354 --> 00:22:43.716
They were very excited.

00:22:43.776 --> 00:22:48.200
Beth, Beth, come quickly, they called.

00:22:48.260 --> 00:22:49.881
You have a present.

00:22:49.941 --> 00:22:51.847
Come and see.

00:22:51.907 --> 00:22:55.133
They took Beth into the living room.

00:22:55.193 --> 00:23:00.214
In the middle of the room was a beautiful little piano.

00:23:00.274 --> 00:23:04.716
On top of the piano, there was an envelope.

00:23:04.776 --> 00:23:07.486
Open the envelope, Beth!

00:23:07.546 --> 00:23:08.937
said Joe.

00:23:08.997 --> 00:23:13.178
Please open it for me, said Beth.

00:23:13.238 --> 00:23:15.678
Joe opened the envelope.

00:23:15.739 --> 00:23:17.789
She pulled out a note.

00:23:17.849 --> 00:23:20.878
She read it to her mother and sisters.

00:23:20.938 --> 00:23:32.200
Dear Miss March, the note said, I have had many pairs of slippers, but your slippers are the best.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:35.862
Thank you for your wonderful present.

00:23:35.922 --> 00:23:38.892
Here is a present from me.

00:23:38.952 --> 00:23:41.143
Please enjoy it.

00:23:41.203 --> 00:23:45.194
Your good friend, James Lawrence.

00:23:45.254 --> 00:23:48.471
Beth was very excited.

00:23:48.531 --> 00:23:53.299
Mr. Lawrence has given me this piano, she said.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:55.962
I am very lucky.

00:23:56.022 --> 00:24:00.524
Beth sat down at the piano and started to play.

00:24:00.584 --> 00:24:07.858
The piano sounded beautiful, but suddenly she stopped playing.

00:24:07.918 --> 00:24:12.602
I must thank Mr. Lawrence now, she said.

00:24:12.662 --> 00:24:15.876
Beth was not shy anymore.

00:24:15.936 --> 00:24:20.770
She ran quickly to the Lawrence house and went inside.

00:24:20.830 --> 00:24:24.102
Mr. Lawrence was in the library.

00:24:24.163 --> 00:24:27.925
Beth ran to him and she kissed him.

00:24:27.985 --> 00:24:36.810
Then she said, dear Mr. Lawrence, thank you so much for my beautiful piano.

00:24:36.870 --> 00:24:48.342
Beth was not afraid of Mr. Lawrence anymore.

00:24:48.402 --> 00:24:57.582
Chapter 5.

00:24:57.642 --> 00:25:01.384
Amy in trouble.

00:25:01.444 --> 00:25:05.186
It was Saturday afternoon.

00:25:05.246 --> 00:25:08.458
Meghan Joe were in their bedroom.

00:25:08.518 --> 00:25:10.899
They were putting on their coats.

00:25:10.959 --> 00:25:13.210
They were going out.

00:25:13.270 --> 00:25:16.390
Amy came into the bedroom.

00:25:16.450 --> 00:25:18.550
Where are you going?

00:25:18.610 --> 00:25:19.811
She asked.

00:25:19.871 --> 00:25:22.994
Don't ask questions, said Joe.

00:25:23.054 --> 00:25:26.940
We're going to the theater with Laurie, said Meg.

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:29.648
We're going to see a play.

00:25:29.708 --> 00:25:32.164
Oh, said Amy.

00:25:32.224 --> 00:25:34.256
I want to come with you.

00:25:34.316 --> 00:25:35.676
Please.

00:25:35.736 --> 00:25:37.778
No, said Joe.

00:25:37.838 --> 00:25:39.928
You are too young.

00:25:39.989 --> 00:25:43.000
I'm not too young, she said.

00:25:43.060 --> 00:25:45.092
I'm 12 years old.

00:25:45.152 --> 00:25:49.494
Please, please let me come with you.

00:25:49.554 --> 00:25:54.148
Joe often became angry very quickly.

00:25:54.208 --> 00:25:57.217
She became very angry with Amy.

00:25:57.277 --> 00:25:59.526
No, Amy," she said.

00:25:59.586 --> 00:26:01.878
We will not take you with us.

00:26:01.938 --> 00:26:04.240
Please go away.

00:26:04.300 --> 00:26:06.892
Amy started to cry.

00:26:06.952 --> 00:26:10.474
At that moment, Laurie arrived at the house.

00:26:10.534 --> 00:26:14.136
Meg, Joe, are you ready?

00:26:14.196 --> 00:26:15.348
He shouted.

00:26:15.408 --> 00:26:18.310
We're coming, Joe replied.

00:26:18.370 --> 00:26:21.492
Joe and Meg ran downstairs.

00:26:21.552 --> 00:26:24.028
Amy stopped crying.

00:26:24.088 --> 00:26:28.877
You'll be sorry, Joe March," she shouted.

00:26:28.937 --> 00:26:33.650
Joe and Meg had a wonderful time at the theater.

00:26:33.711 --> 00:26:36.554
They were turned home in the evening.

00:26:36.614 --> 00:26:39.146
Amy was reading a book.

00:26:39.206 --> 00:26:43.780
She did not ask them questions about the play.

00:26:43.840 --> 00:26:49.895
The next day, Meg, Beth, and Amy were sitting in the living room.

00:26:49.956 --> 00:26:52.535
They were sitting by the fire.

00:26:52.595 --> 00:26:55.654
Suddenly Joe ran into the room.

00:26:55.714 --> 00:26:58.215
She was very upset.

00:26:58.275 --> 00:27:00.806
Where is my book of stories?

00:27:00.866 --> 00:27:02.727
She asked her sisters.

00:27:02.787 --> 00:27:04.918
Have you seen it?

00:27:04.978 --> 00:27:07.999
Joe often wrote stories.

00:27:08.059 --> 00:27:11.000
She wrote them all in a little book.

00:27:11.060 --> 00:27:14.682
But today she could not find her book.

00:27:14.742 --> 00:27:18.453
I haven't seen your book, said Meg.

00:27:18.513 --> 00:27:20.624
Have you seen it, Beth?

00:27:20.684 --> 00:27:23.445
No, said Beth.

00:27:23.505 --> 00:27:26.276
Amy was very quiet.

00:27:26.336 --> 00:27:29.317
She did not say anything.

00:27:29.377 --> 00:27:32.828
Amy, where is my book of stories?

00:27:32.888 --> 00:27:34.359
asked Joe.

00:27:34.419 --> 00:27:37.450
I don't know, replied Amy.

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:40.701
Yes, you do know, said Joe.

00:27:40.761 --> 00:27:42.822
Tell me immediately.

00:27:42.882 --> 00:27:44.532
Where is it?

00:27:44.592 --> 00:27:48.744
You'll never see it again, said Amy.

00:27:48.804 --> 00:27:50.184
Why not?

00:27:50.244 --> 00:27:51.654
asked Joe.

00:27:51.714 --> 00:27:54.494
I burnt it, said Amy.

00:27:54.554 --> 00:28:01.607
You didn't let me come to the theater yesterday, so I threw your book of stories on the fire."

00:28:01.668 --> 00:28:04.559
Joe was very angry.

00:28:04.620 --> 00:28:08.012
She held Amy's arms and shouted at her.

00:28:08.072 --> 00:28:11.103
You bad, bad girl!

00:28:11.163 --> 00:28:12.504
Joe shouted.

00:28:12.564 --> 00:28:15.406
I wrote those stories for father.

00:28:15.466 --> 00:28:18.198
Now they are gone forever.

00:28:18.258 --> 00:28:21.190
Suddenly, Amy was sorry.

00:28:21.250 --> 00:28:23.382
She started to cry.

00:28:23.442 --> 00:28:27.364
Please forgive me, Joe," Amy said.

00:28:27.424 --> 00:28:30.246
I'm very, very sorry.

00:28:30.306 --> 00:28:32.597
Tears fell from her eyes.

00:28:32.657 --> 00:28:36.130
I'll never forgive you, said Joe.

00:28:36.190 --> 00:28:38.221
Never!

00:28:38.280 --> 00:28:42.534
Joe did not speak to Amy again that day.

00:28:42.594 --> 00:28:47.220
She was very angry and upset.

00:28:47.280 --> 00:28:52.608
The next day the weather was very cold.

00:28:52.668 --> 00:28:55.720
There was a river near the March's house.

00:28:55.780 --> 00:28:57.912
The river had frozen.

00:28:57.972 --> 00:29:00.173
It was ice.

00:29:00.233 --> 00:29:03.395
Lori came to the March's house.

00:29:03.455 --> 00:29:06.438
He was carrying a pair of ice skates.

00:29:06.498 --> 00:29:09.710
Let's go to the river, Joe, he said.

00:29:09.770 --> 00:29:11.792
We'll skate on the ice.

00:29:11.852 --> 00:29:14.394
All right, replied Joe.

00:29:14.454 --> 00:29:19.051
She went to a cupboard and she took out her ice skates.

00:29:19.111 --> 00:29:22.188
Amy watched her sister.

00:29:22.248 --> 00:29:26.941
After a few minutes, Joe and Laurie left the house.

00:29:27.001 --> 00:29:31.594
I want to skate too, Amy said to Meg.

00:29:31.654 --> 00:29:36.108
Take your ice skates and run after Joe, said Meg.

00:29:36.168 --> 00:29:38.299
Joe will enjoy herself.

00:29:38.359 --> 00:29:40.650
She will soon be happy.

00:29:40.710 --> 00:29:43.512
Ask her to be your friend again.

00:29:43.572 --> 00:29:48.134
That is a good idea, said Amy.

00:29:48.194 --> 00:29:52.014
She ran after Joe and Laurie.

00:29:52.074 --> 00:29:55.158
The river was not far away.

00:29:55.218 --> 00:29:59.962
Soon she saw Joe and Laurie skating on the ice.

00:30:00.022 --> 00:30:03.596
Quickly, she put on her ice skates.

00:30:03.656 --> 00:30:07.900
The ice was very thin in the middle of the river.

00:30:07.960 --> 00:30:11.184
Don't go to the middle of the river, Joe.

00:30:11.244 --> 00:30:13.366
Laurie said to Joe.

00:30:13.426 --> 00:30:16.518
Joe heard Lori's words.

00:30:16.578 --> 00:30:19.899
But Amy did not hear Lori.

00:30:19.959 --> 00:30:23.140
She skated to the middle of the river.

00:30:23.200 --> 00:30:26.702
Suddenly there was a loud crack.

00:30:26.762 --> 00:30:29.062
The ice broke.

00:30:29.122 --> 00:30:31.513
Amy was in the water.

00:30:31.573 --> 00:30:33.314
Help me, Joe.

00:30:33.374 --> 00:30:34.584
She shouted.

00:30:34.644 --> 00:30:37.825
Lori skated quickly towards Amy.

00:30:37.885 --> 00:30:39.496
Quickly, Joe.

00:30:39.556 --> 00:30:41.676
Quickly, he shouted.

00:30:41.736 --> 00:30:44.284
We must pull her out.

00:30:44.344 --> 00:30:50.415
Joe was terribly afraid, but she followed Laurie.

00:30:50.475 --> 00:30:54.137
They pulled Amy from the river.

00:30:54.198 --> 00:31:00.742
Amy was not hurt, but she was very cold and frightened.

00:31:00.802 --> 00:31:04.546
Joe and Laurie took Amy home.

00:31:04.606 --> 00:31:08.678
Mrs. March carried Amy upstairs to her bedroom.

00:31:08.738 --> 00:31:14.761
She took off the little girl's wet clothes, and she wrapped her in a blanket.

00:31:14.821 --> 00:31:19.192
Then she carried her downstairs to the living room.

00:31:19.252 --> 00:31:23.404
Amy fell asleep by the warm fire.

00:31:23.464 --> 00:31:27.116
Will Amy be all right, Marmy?

00:31:27.176 --> 00:31:28.776
asked Joe.

00:31:28.836 --> 00:31:32.248
Yes, dear, replied her mother.

00:31:32.308 --> 00:31:36.631
Amy was in trouble, but she will be all right now.

00:31:36.691 --> 00:31:38.702
She isn't hurt.

00:31:38.762 --> 00:31:41.704
Joe started to cry.

00:31:41.764 --> 00:31:45.958
I was angry with Amy, said Joe.

00:31:46.019 --> 00:31:48.852
She burnt my book of stories.

00:31:48.912 --> 00:31:52.304
But now I am very sorry.

00:31:52.365 --> 00:31:56.317
Sometimes I become angry too quickly.

00:31:56.378 --> 00:31:58.560
What shall I do, Marmy?

00:31:58.620 --> 00:32:00.632
Please help me.

00:32:00.692 --> 00:32:04.744
Don't cry, Joe, said Mrs. March.

00:32:04.804 --> 00:32:07.207
Remember this day.

00:32:07.267 --> 00:32:10.444
You won't become angry again.

00:32:10.504 --> 00:32:14.791
I will remember," said Joe.

00:32:14.851 --> 00:32:20.596
At that moment, Amy opened her eyes, and she smiled.

00:32:20.656 --> 00:32:23.918
She held out her arms towards Joe.

00:32:23.978 --> 00:32:30.754
The two sisters did not speak, but they kissed and they put their arms around each other.

00:32:30.814 --> 00:32:34.086
They were friends again.

00:32:34.146 --> 00:32:37.640
Winter soon passed.

00:32:37.700 --> 00:32:40.562
Spring came and then summer.

00:32:40.622 --> 00:32:43.775
Mrs. March and her daughters were happy.

00:32:43.835 --> 00:32:50.346
But they all wanted to see Mr. March again soon.

00:32:50.406 --> 00:33:04.392
Chapter 6 Meg loses a glove.

00:33:04.452 --> 00:33:15.650
Meg, the eldest March sister, was a very pretty girl.

00:33:15.710 --> 00:33:19.331
Her friends often invited her to parties.

00:33:19.391 --> 00:33:25.004
Meg enjoyed the parties, but sometimes she was sad.

00:33:25.064 --> 00:33:29.046
She was sad because her family was poor.

00:33:29.106 --> 00:33:32.377
Meg's friends lived in fine houses.

00:33:32.437 --> 00:33:39.912
They had beautiful clothes, but Meg did not have beautiful clothes and lovely things.

00:33:39.972 --> 00:33:45.217
One day in July, Meg was at a friend's house.

00:33:45.277 --> 00:33:47.838
She heard a conversation.

00:33:47.898 --> 00:33:53.430
Two women were talking, her friend's mother and another woman.

00:33:53.490 --> 00:33:56.812
They were talking about Meg.

00:33:56.872 --> 00:34:02.984
Meg March is a kind and lovely girl, said one woman.

00:34:03.044 --> 00:34:06.296
But her family is poor.

00:34:06.356 --> 00:34:09.626
The marches live near the Lawrence's.

00:34:09.687 --> 00:34:11.556
said the other woman.

00:34:11.616 --> 00:34:14.978
The Lawrence's are very rich.

00:34:15.038 --> 00:34:19.799
Does Mrs. March have marriage plans for her daughters?

00:34:19.859 --> 00:34:24.780
Will one of them marry Mr. Lawrence's grandson?

00:34:24.841 --> 00:34:30.158
Meg heard these words, and she was very upset.

00:34:30.218 --> 00:34:34.188
I like Laurie very much," she thought.

00:34:34.248 --> 00:34:37.110
But I do not want to marry him.

00:34:37.170 --> 00:34:40.031
We don't think about Laurie's money.

00:34:40.091 --> 00:34:42.612
He is our best friend.

00:34:42.673 --> 00:34:44.754
Meg went home.

00:34:44.814 --> 00:34:47.096
She spoke to her mother.

00:34:47.156 --> 00:34:51.579
Marme, do you have marriage plans for us?

00:34:51.639 --> 00:34:53.070
She asked.

00:34:53.130 --> 00:34:55.001
Marriage plans?

00:34:55.061 --> 00:34:56.887
said Mrs. March.

00:34:56.947 --> 00:35:01.536
Meg told her mother all about the women's conversation.

00:35:01.596 --> 00:35:04.670
Mrs. March was very angry.

00:35:04.730 --> 00:35:08.912
Those women are very foolish, she said.

00:35:08.972 --> 00:35:13.446
My daughters are beautiful and good and happy.

00:35:13.506 --> 00:35:16.540
They will marry good husbands.

00:35:16.600 --> 00:35:22.484
But good men are not always rich men, Mrs. March said.

00:35:22.544 --> 00:35:26.316
Love is more important than money.

00:35:26.376 --> 00:35:31.065
Don't marry a rich man without love, Meg.

00:35:31.126 --> 00:35:34.936
Marry a poor man with love.

00:35:34.996 --> 00:35:37.588
Then you will be happy.

00:35:37.648 --> 00:35:41.479
You're right, Marmy, Meg said.

00:35:41.539 --> 00:35:45.830
I'll always remember your words.

00:35:45.890 --> 00:35:51.192
The next day, a letter arrived for Joe.

00:35:51.252 --> 00:35:54.985
Joe read the letter to her sisters.

00:35:55.045 --> 00:36:03.482
Dear Joe," the letter said, tomorrow some new friends will come to visit me.

00:36:03.542 --> 00:36:07.044
We will go on a picnic by the river.

00:36:07.104 --> 00:36:09.366
I have two boats.

00:36:09.426 --> 00:36:12.168
We will have a good day.

00:36:12.228 --> 00:36:16.240
John Brooke, my teacher, will come with us.

00:36:16.300 --> 00:36:22.274
Please come, and please bring Meg, Beth, and Amy too.

00:36:22.334 --> 00:36:26.158
Best wishes, Laurie.

00:36:26.218 --> 00:36:30.241
That will be exciting, said Amy.

00:36:30.301 --> 00:36:34.142
Please, Marmy, we want to go on the picnic."

00:36:34.202 --> 00:36:35.693
Very well.

00:36:35.753 --> 00:36:38.924
Go on the picnic, said Mrs. March.

00:36:38.984 --> 00:36:42.336
You will have a good time.

00:36:42.396 --> 00:36:46.657
The next day was warm and sunny.

00:36:46.717 --> 00:36:50.458
Laurie and his new friends walked to the river.

00:36:50.518 --> 00:36:53.449
The March girls met them there.

00:36:53.509 --> 00:36:56.697
They all brought baskets of food.

00:36:56.758 --> 00:37:00.846
They put the baskets into the two small boats.

00:37:00.906 --> 00:37:03.908
The March sisters sat in the boats.

00:37:03.968 --> 00:37:07.720
Lori and his friends rode the boats on the river.

00:37:07.780 --> 00:37:12.782
Then they got out and they found a good place for the picnic.

00:37:12.842 --> 00:37:17.853
Everybody was hungry and the food was delicious.

00:37:17.914 --> 00:37:27.222
Later, Joe, Lori, Beth, and Amy talked to Lori's friends and they played games.

00:37:27.283 --> 00:37:30.739
Meg was reading a German book.

00:37:30.800 --> 00:37:34.182
She did not understand some of the words.

00:37:34.242 --> 00:37:39.254
Mr. Brooke, Lori's teacher, understood German.

00:37:39.314 --> 00:37:42.415
He helped Meg with the words.

00:37:42.476 --> 00:37:46.268
Mr. Brooke was a quiet young man.

00:37:46.328 --> 00:37:50.020
He had brown eyes and a kind face.

00:37:50.080 --> 00:37:55.935
He often looked at Meg, but Meg did not see him looking at her.

00:37:55.996 --> 00:38:00.800
You're a very good teacher, Mr. Brooke, said Meg.

00:38:00.860 --> 00:38:04.131
Thank you, replied Mr. Brooke.

00:38:04.191 --> 00:38:06.152
I enjoy my work.

00:38:06.212 --> 00:38:09.674
Laurie is a very good student.

00:38:09.734 --> 00:38:13.766
Everybody had a good time at the picnic.

00:38:13.826 --> 00:38:18.548
At last, they had to go home.

00:38:18.608 --> 00:38:25.044
The next day, Meg was looking for her gloves.

00:38:25.104 --> 00:38:28.770
I've lost a glove, she said.

00:38:28.830 --> 00:38:30.771
Have you seen it, Joe?

00:38:30.831 --> 00:38:34.333
No, I haven't seen it, replied Joe.

00:38:34.393 --> 00:38:36.494
Did you lose it at the picnic?

00:38:36.554 --> 00:38:38.755
I'll ask Laurie.

00:38:38.815 --> 00:38:44.448
Later, Joe said to Laurie, Meg has lost a glove.

00:38:44.508 --> 00:38:46.939
Laurie started to laugh.

00:38:46.999 --> 00:38:50.520
I know where her glove is, he said.

00:38:50.580 --> 00:38:53.752
Where is it, asked Joe?

00:38:53.812 --> 00:38:55.588
I will tell you.

00:38:55.649 --> 00:38:56.724
said Laurie.

00:38:56.784 --> 00:38:58.445
But don't tell Meg.

00:38:58.465 --> 00:39:02.636
I won't tell Meg, said Joe.

00:39:02.696 --> 00:39:08.637
The glove is in John Brooke's pocket, said Laurie.

00:39:08.697 --> 00:39:11.438
Joe did not understand.

00:39:11.498 --> 00:39:14.298
What do you mean, she said?

00:39:14.358 --> 00:39:17.989
Why is the glove in John Brooke's pocket?

00:39:18.049 --> 00:39:23.578
Meg dropped her glove and John Brooke found it, said Laurie.

00:39:23.638 --> 00:39:26.396
He put the glove in his pocket.

00:39:26.456 --> 00:39:28.896
He looks at it every day.

00:39:28.956 --> 00:39:31.467
John is in love with Meg.

00:39:31.527 --> 00:39:33.757
Isn't that wonderful?

00:39:33.817 --> 00:39:37.198
But Joe was angry and upset.

00:39:37.258 --> 00:39:39.529
No, she said.

00:39:39.589 --> 00:39:41.499
It isn't wonderful.

00:39:41.559 --> 00:39:43.490
It's terrible news.

00:39:43.550 --> 00:39:46.020
Mr. Brooke will marry Meg.

00:39:46.080 --> 00:39:48.431
He will take her away from us.

00:39:48.491 --> 00:39:51.282
No, I am not happy.

00:39:51.342 --> 00:40:02.392
I am very unhappy.

00:40:02.453 --> 00:40:18.916
Chapter 7 A Telegram Summer and autumn passed.

00:40:18.976 --> 00:40:20.637
It was November.

00:40:20.697 --> 00:40:24.123
The weather was cold and wet.

00:40:24.183 --> 00:40:29.652
One afternoon, the March sisters were sitting in their living room.

00:40:29.712 --> 00:40:32.083
Meg looked out of the window.

00:40:32.144 --> 00:40:34.415
She watched the rain.

00:40:34.475 --> 00:40:38.898
November is a terrible month, she said.

00:40:38.958 --> 00:40:41.460
It is cold and wet.

00:40:41.520 --> 00:40:43.822
Nothing ever happens.

00:40:43.882 --> 00:40:48.996
Our lives are very boring, and we have no money.

00:40:49.056 --> 00:40:52.192
Amy was painting a picture.

00:40:52.252 --> 00:40:56.868
One day I'll be a famous artist, she said.

00:40:56.928 --> 00:40:58.759
I'll travel to Italy.

00:40:58.779 --> 00:41:02.000
I'll paint beautiful pictures.

00:41:02.060 --> 00:41:04.400
Then I'll sell the pictures.

00:41:04.460 --> 00:41:07.481
And we will have lots of money.

00:41:07.541 --> 00:41:11.402
I'm going to write books, said Joe.

00:41:11.462 --> 00:41:14.223
I'll be rich and famous too.

00:41:14.283 --> 00:41:16.274
That is my dream.

00:41:16.334 --> 00:41:19.040
What is your dream, Beth?

00:41:19.100 --> 00:41:23.060
I'm very happy now," said Beth.

00:41:23.120 --> 00:41:26.852
I shall stay at home with Marmy and Father.

00:41:26.912 --> 00:41:30.055
Meg looked out of the window again.

00:41:30.115 --> 00:41:33.547
Suddenly she said, there's Laurie.

00:41:33.608 --> 00:41:36.570
He's coming to the front door.

00:41:36.630 --> 00:41:41.234
A few moments later, Laurie came into the room.

00:41:41.294 --> 00:41:44.726
He was holding a small envelope in his hand.

00:41:44.786 --> 00:41:47.341
He was worried and upset.

00:41:47.401 --> 00:41:49.295
What is it, Laurie?

00:41:49.355 --> 00:41:50.546
said Joe.

00:41:50.607 --> 00:41:52.528
Is something wrong?

00:41:52.588 --> 00:41:54.670
Where is Mrs. March?

00:41:54.730 --> 00:41:56.001
said Laurie.

00:41:56.061 --> 00:41:58.804
I have come from the post office.

00:41:58.864 --> 00:42:01.676
Laurie held up the envelope.

00:42:01.736 --> 00:42:04.548
This is a telegram for your mother.

00:42:04.609 --> 00:42:07.972
It's from Washington, he said.

00:42:08.032 --> 00:42:12.206
At that moment, Mrs. March came into the room.

00:42:12.266 --> 00:42:15.096
Laurie gave her the telegram.

00:42:15.156 --> 00:42:19.417
Mrs. March opened it, and she read it quickly.

00:42:19.477 --> 00:42:22.208
Then she sat down in a chair.

00:42:22.268 --> 00:42:24.960
Her face was white.

00:42:25.020 --> 00:42:29.572
The telegram was from a hospital in Washington.

00:42:29.632 --> 00:42:34.656
Your husband is very ill, the telegram said.

00:42:34.716 --> 00:42:37.086
He is in this hospital.

00:42:37.146 --> 00:42:39.038
Come immediately.

00:42:39.098 --> 00:42:39.948
P.

00:42:40.008 --> 00:42:45.190
Dale, the Army Hospital, Washington.

00:42:45.250 --> 00:42:50.752
I must go to Washington," said Mrs. March.

00:42:50.812 --> 00:42:53.944
I will go on the train tomorrow morning.

00:42:54.004 --> 00:43:01.706
Joe, run to the post office, send a telegram to the hospital, send this reply.

00:43:01.726 --> 00:43:05.018
I will come immediately.

00:43:05.078 --> 00:43:09.789
Meg, Beth, Amy, come and help me.

00:43:09.849 --> 00:43:13.845
I have to pack my case.

00:43:13.905 --> 00:43:18.702
The three girls started to help their mother.

00:43:18.763 --> 00:43:21.906
Joe put on her hat and she went out.

00:43:21.966 --> 00:43:24.798
Laurie went home.

00:43:24.858 --> 00:43:29.351
Mrs. March went to her desk in the living room.

00:43:29.412 --> 00:43:31.424
She opened a drawer.

00:43:31.484 --> 00:43:34.076
There was some money in the drawer.

00:43:34.136 --> 00:43:36.268
She looked at the money.

00:43:36.328 --> 00:43:39.160
There was not very much.

00:43:39.221 --> 00:43:43.448
I have to buy a train ticket, she thought.

00:43:43.508 --> 00:43:47.523
Will the girls have enough money for food?

00:43:47.583 --> 00:43:52.724
A few minutes later there was a knock on the front door.

00:43:52.784 --> 00:43:55.675
Meg opened the door.

00:43:55.735 --> 00:44:02.707
Old Mr. Lawrence and Mr. Brooke, Laurie's teacher, were standing outside.

00:44:02.767 --> 00:44:07.508
Laurie told us the bad news about your father.

00:44:07.568 --> 00:44:11.546
Said Mr. Lawrence, I'm very sorry.

00:44:11.607 --> 00:44:14.475
Will your mother go to Washington?

00:44:14.535 --> 00:44:16.936
Yes, said Meg.

00:44:16.996 --> 00:44:20.478
She will go to Washington tomorrow morning.

00:44:20.538 --> 00:44:24.979
She must not go alone, said Mr. Lawrence.

00:44:25.039 --> 00:44:27.780
A friend must go with her.

00:44:27.840 --> 00:44:30.031
I'm an old man.

00:44:30.091 --> 00:44:31.922
I am not strong.

00:44:31.982 --> 00:44:34.252
I can't go with her.

00:44:34.312 --> 00:44:37.484
But John Brooke is a young man.

00:44:37.544 --> 00:44:41.078
He can go to Washington with your mother.

00:44:41.138 --> 00:44:45.294
Mr. Brooke looked at Meg, and he smiled.

00:44:45.354 --> 00:44:48.045
His face was very kind.

00:44:48.106 --> 00:44:51.538
Don't worry about your mother, he said.

00:44:51.598 --> 00:44:53.580
I'll take care of her.

00:44:53.640 --> 00:44:56.191
Meg was very pleased.

00:44:56.251 --> 00:45:01.094
Thank you very, very much, she said.

00:45:01.154 --> 00:45:05.967
Soon everything was ready for Mrs. March's journey.

00:45:06.027 --> 00:45:10.465
Evening came, but Joe had not returned.

00:45:10.525 --> 00:45:13.130
Mrs. March was worried.

00:45:13.190 --> 00:45:15.111
Where is Joe?

00:45:15.171 --> 00:45:16.272
She said.

00:45:16.332 --> 00:45:18.772
It's very late.

00:45:18.832 --> 00:45:22.243
At last, Joe came home.

00:45:22.303 --> 00:45:27.264
She walked into the kitchen, and she put some money on the table.

00:45:27.324 --> 00:45:30.636
This money is for your journey, Marmy.

00:45:30.696 --> 00:45:32.326
She said.

00:45:32.386 --> 00:45:35.247
Mrs. March looked at the money.

00:45:35.307 --> 00:45:37.467
Then she looked at Joe.

00:45:37.527 --> 00:45:40.401
She was very surprised.

00:45:40.461 --> 00:45:44.326
Twenty-five dollars, she said.

00:45:44.386 --> 00:45:48.267
Joe, where did you get this money?

00:45:48.327 --> 00:45:50.838
Joe did not answer.

00:45:50.898 --> 00:45:53.139
She took off her hat.

00:45:53.199 --> 00:45:55.620
Everybody looked at her.

00:45:55.680 --> 00:45:58.971
Joe's hair was very short.

00:45:59.032 --> 00:46:04.574
Your hair, your beautiful red hair, said Meg.

00:46:04.634 --> 00:46:08.943
Oh, Joe, what have you done?

00:46:09.003 --> 00:46:14.114
Many women want long red hair, said Joe.

00:46:14.174 --> 00:46:16.326
I went to the barber's shop.

00:46:16.386 --> 00:46:18.477
The barber cut my hair.

00:46:18.537 --> 00:46:20.848
Then I sold him my hair.

00:46:20.908 --> 00:46:23.741
He gave me $25 for it.

00:46:23.801 --> 00:46:27.004
I wanted to help Marmy and Father.

00:46:27.063 --> 00:46:30.736
Tears fell from Mrs. March's eyes.

00:46:30.796 --> 00:46:36.792
Joe, you are good and kind, she said.

00:46:36.852 --> 00:46:42.018
That night, Meg and Joe could not sleep.

00:46:42.078 --> 00:46:45.150
Joe was thinking about her hair.

00:46:45.210 --> 00:46:49.103
Meg was thinking about Mr. Brooke.

00:46:49.164 --> 00:46:54.217
Both girls were worrying about their father.

00:46:54.278 --> 00:47:00.732
The next morning, Mr. Lawrence's carriage came to the March's house.

00:47:00.792 --> 00:47:04.216
Mr. Brooke was sitting inside the carriage.

00:47:04.276 --> 00:47:08.738
Mrs. March kissed her daughters, and she said goodbye.

00:47:08.798 --> 00:47:11.860
Then she got into the carriage.

00:47:11.920 --> 00:47:17.082
The sun shone on the sad faces of the March sisters.

00:47:17.142 --> 00:47:21.214
Goodbye, dear Mommy, they said.

00:47:21.274 --> 00:47:32.519
Goodbye.

00:47:32.579 --> 00:47:47.534
Chapter 8 Beth is ill.

00:47:47.594 --> 00:47:51.315
Mrs. March was in Washington.

00:47:51.376 --> 00:47:54.856
The four sisters worked very hard.

00:47:54.917 --> 00:47:57.947
They did the housework every day.

00:47:58.007 --> 00:48:08.967
They were worried about their father and mother, but the girls were very kind to each other, and they wrote to their mother every day.

00:48:09.028 --> 00:48:14.118
Soon a letter arrived from Mrs. March.

00:48:14.178 --> 00:48:21.672
My dear daughters, the letter said, I have some wonderful news.

00:48:21.732 --> 00:48:26.895
Father is getting better, but he is not strong.

00:48:26.955 --> 00:48:30.737
He has to stay in hospital for some weeks.

00:48:30.797 --> 00:48:34.330
Then Mr. Brooke and I will bring him home.

00:48:34.390 --> 00:48:37.231
Don't worry, little daughters.

00:48:37.291 --> 00:48:39.646
Take care of each other.

00:48:39.706 --> 00:48:43.382
Soon we will all be together again.

00:48:43.442 --> 00:48:46.704
Your loving Marmee.

00:48:46.764 --> 00:48:55.450
The girls were happy, and soon Meg, Joe, and Amy forgot about the housework.

00:48:55.510 --> 00:48:58.322
Beth did not forget.

00:48:58.382 --> 00:49:04.386
She did her own work, and she did her sister's work too.

00:49:04.446 --> 00:49:10.399
One afternoon, Beth, Meg, and Joe were talking.

00:49:10.459 --> 00:49:13.210
Amy was not at home.

00:49:13.270 --> 00:49:16.112
Meg, said Beth.

00:49:16.172 --> 00:49:19.405
Please, will you visit the Hummel family?

00:49:19.465 --> 00:49:21.887
Marmy often visits them.

00:49:21.947 --> 00:49:24.128
Marmy is not here.

00:49:24.188 --> 00:49:27.002
We must visit the Hummel's.

00:49:27.062 --> 00:49:29.063
I'm sorry, Beth.

00:49:29.123 --> 00:49:32.476
I'm very tired today, said Meg.

00:49:32.536 --> 00:49:35.348
Joe must go to the Hummel's house.

00:49:35.408 --> 00:49:38.120
I can't go, said Joe.

00:49:38.180 --> 00:49:40.271
I'm going to meet Laurie.

00:49:40.331 --> 00:49:43.011
I can't visit the Hummels today.

00:49:43.071 --> 00:49:45.882
You must go yourself, Beth."

00:49:45.942 --> 00:49:51.266
I visited the Hummels every day this week, said Beth.

00:49:51.326 --> 00:49:55.608
The baby is ill, and I am very worried.

00:49:55.668 --> 00:49:58.120
Oh, said Meg.

00:49:58.180 --> 00:50:04.062
Amy will come home soon, then she must visit the Hummels.

00:50:04.122 --> 00:50:09.610
An hour passed, but Amy did not come home.

00:50:09.670 --> 00:50:12.767
Meghan Joe went upstairs.

00:50:12.827 --> 00:50:15.518
Meg looked at a new dress.

00:50:15.578 --> 00:50:17.909
Joe wrote a story.

00:50:17.970 --> 00:50:20.760
They forgot about the hummels.

00:50:20.821 --> 00:50:23.032
Beth waited.

00:50:23.092 --> 00:50:25.873
At last she put on her coat.

00:50:25.933 --> 00:50:29.874
She put some food in a basket and she went out.

00:50:29.935 --> 00:50:33.946
Meghan Joe did not see her leaving.

00:50:34.006 --> 00:50:37.386
Later Beth returned.

00:50:37.446 --> 00:50:40.268
She did not speak to anybody.

00:50:40.328 --> 00:50:45.310
She went upstairs to her mother's bedroom, and she shut the door.

00:50:45.370 --> 00:50:49.482
An hour later, Joe found Beth.

00:50:49.542 --> 00:50:52.564
Beth was sitting on her mother's bed.

00:50:52.624 --> 00:50:56.806
Her face was white, and she was crying.

00:50:56.866 --> 00:50:59.898
She was holding a bottle of medicine.

00:50:59.958 --> 00:51:01.780
What is wrong?"

00:51:01.840 --> 00:51:03.150
Joe asked.

00:51:03.210 --> 00:51:07.934
Oh, Joe, the baby is dead, said Beth.

00:51:07.994 --> 00:51:11.166
Which baby asked Joe?

00:51:11.226 --> 00:51:14.629
The Hummel baby replied Beth.

00:51:14.689 --> 00:51:17.931
I went to the Hummel's house this afternoon.

00:51:17.992 --> 00:51:20.544
The baby was very ill.

00:51:20.604 --> 00:51:23.356
Mrs. Hummel went to get the doctor.

00:51:23.416 --> 00:51:27.760
I held the baby in my arms, but it died.

00:51:27.820 --> 00:51:32.103
Oh, Beth, that is terrible, said Joe.

00:51:32.164 --> 00:51:34.394
What happened next?

00:51:34.455 --> 00:51:38.766
Mrs. Hummel came back with the doctor, said Beth.

00:51:38.826 --> 00:51:41.127
The doctor looked at the baby.

00:51:41.188 --> 00:51:45.389
He said, this baby had scarlet fever.

00:51:45.449 --> 00:51:48.580
scarlet fever, said Joe.

00:51:48.640 --> 00:51:51.092
Yes, Beth said.

00:51:51.152 --> 00:51:53.950
The doctor gave me this medicine.

00:51:54.010 --> 00:51:58.670
He said, go home immediately, drink some of this.

00:51:58.730 --> 00:52:03.084
And now I have a headache, and I'm very hot.

00:52:03.144 --> 00:52:05.898
Suddenly Joe was afraid.

00:52:05.958 --> 00:52:08.580
Has Beth got scarlet fever?

00:52:08.640 --> 00:52:09.720
She thought.

00:52:09.781 --> 00:52:13.724
It is a very dangerous illness.

00:52:13.784 --> 00:52:17.627
Don't worry Beth, Joe said.

00:52:17.688 --> 00:52:21.852
I'll tell Meg, we will get Marme's doctor.

00:52:21.912 --> 00:52:24.965
Meg was very worried.

00:52:25.025 --> 00:52:29.997
Beth went to the Hummel's house every day, she said to Joe.

00:52:30.057 --> 00:52:34.008
We must get Dr. Bang's immediately.

00:52:34.068 --> 00:52:38.230
Dr. Bang's came, and he looked at Beth.

00:52:38.290 --> 00:52:41.922
Then the doctor spoke to Meg and Joe.

00:52:41.982 --> 00:52:45.673
Beth has scarlet fever, he said.

00:52:45.733 --> 00:52:47.870
Who will take care of her?

00:52:47.930 --> 00:52:50.346
We will," said Meg.

00:52:50.406 --> 00:52:53.108
Joe and I have had scarlet fever.

00:52:53.168 --> 00:52:54.818
We are safe.

00:52:54.878 --> 00:52:57.840
Has Amy had scarlet fever?

00:52:57.900 --> 00:53:00.012
asked Dr. Bangs.

00:53:00.072 --> 00:53:03.894
Amy hasn't had the fever, replied Meg.

00:53:03.954 --> 00:53:06.284
She will not be safe here.

00:53:06.344 --> 00:53:10.176
She must stay with Father's aunt, Aunt March.

00:53:10.236 --> 00:53:12.978
Good, said Dr. Bangs.

00:53:13.038 --> 00:53:14.839
Take care of Beth.

00:53:14.899 --> 00:53:17.540
I'll come again tomorrow.

00:53:17.600 --> 00:53:20.550
The doctor left the house.

00:53:20.610 --> 00:53:22.841
Joe spoke to Meg.

00:53:22.901 --> 00:53:26.121
We must write to Marme, she said.

00:53:26.181 --> 00:53:28.572
We must tell her about Beth.

00:53:28.632 --> 00:53:30.992
No, said Meg.

00:53:31.052 --> 00:53:33.783
Marme is taking care of father.

00:53:33.843 --> 00:53:36.083
She can't come home now.

00:53:36.143 --> 00:53:38.934
Marme must stay in Washington.

00:53:38.994 --> 00:53:42.384
We must not tell her about Beth.

00:53:42.444 --> 00:53:45.212
Joe started to cry.

00:53:45.272 --> 00:53:49.490
Washington is many miles away," she said.

00:53:49.550 --> 00:53:51.831
We were wrong, Meg.

00:53:51.891 --> 00:53:54.372
We didn't visit the Hummels.

00:53:54.432 --> 00:54:00.085
Beth went there every day, and now she has scarlet fever.

00:54:00.146 --> 00:54:03.730
Oh, Meg, what are we going to do?

00:54:03.790 --> 00:54:06.866
Meg put her arms round Joe.

00:54:06.926 --> 00:54:10.058
Don't cry Joe, she said.

00:54:10.118 --> 00:54:14.924
Beth has scarlet fever, but she will get better soon.

00:54:14.984 --> 00:54:18.378
Now we must take care of her.

00:54:18.438 --> 00:54:23.294
The next day, Amy went to Aunt March's house.

00:54:23.354 --> 00:54:35.489
Meg and Joe took care of Beth.

00:54:35.549 --> 00:54:57.424
Chapter 9 News from Washington Beth was very ill, the days passed and she did not get better.

00:54:57.484 --> 00:54:59.743
Beth could not eat.

00:54:59.803 --> 00:55:02.545
She slept for many hours.

00:55:02.606 --> 00:55:07.768
Sometimes she was awake, but she could not remember things.

00:55:07.828 --> 00:55:11.332
Sometimes she called Joe Meg.

00:55:11.392 --> 00:55:15.103
Sometimes she called Meg Joe.

00:55:15.164 --> 00:55:19.557
Beth said her mother's name again and again.

00:55:19.617 --> 00:55:23.220
Joe and Meg were worried and afraid.

00:55:23.280 --> 00:55:27.560
One morning, the two girls were talking.

00:55:27.620 --> 00:55:32.270
Let's send a telegram to Marme, said Joe.

00:55:32.330 --> 00:55:34.961
Let's tell her about Beth now.

00:55:35.021 --> 00:55:37.262
Then she will come home.

00:55:37.322 --> 00:55:40.274
All right, said Meg.

00:55:40.334 --> 00:55:44.978
She sat down and she wrote the words for a telegram.

00:55:45.038 --> 00:55:51.096
Dearest Marme, she wrote, Beth has scarlet fever.

00:55:51.156 --> 00:55:53.378
She is very ill.

00:55:53.438 --> 00:55:56.180
Please come home immediately.

00:55:56.240 --> 00:56:00.704
Your loving daughters, Meg and Joe."

00:56:00.764 --> 00:56:06.549
I'll take this to the post office this afternoon," said Meg.

00:56:06.609 --> 00:56:11.674
But that afternoon a letter arrived from Mrs. March.

00:56:11.734 --> 00:56:14.586
There was bad news in the letter.

00:56:14.646 --> 00:56:18.470
Mr. March was very ill again.

00:56:18.530 --> 00:56:21.574
Meghan Joe read the letter.

00:56:21.634 --> 00:56:23.905
They looked at each other.

00:56:23.965 --> 00:56:28.987
We must not send the telegram to Marmy, said Meghan.

00:56:29.047 --> 00:56:33.409
Bath is ill, but father is ill too.

00:56:33.469 --> 00:56:36.180
Marmy must stay with him.

00:56:36.240 --> 00:56:39.601
She can't come home now.

00:56:39.662 --> 00:56:44.224
A week later, it was the first day of December.

00:56:44.284 --> 00:56:51.036
The weather was very cold, the wind blew all day, and snow fell.

00:56:51.096 --> 00:56:55.289
In the morning, Dr. Bangs visited the house.

00:56:55.349 --> 00:56:58.830
He looked at Beth for a long time.

00:56:58.890 --> 00:57:01.962
Then he spoke to Meg and Joe.

00:57:02.022 --> 00:57:05.704
Beth is very, very ill.

00:57:05.764 --> 00:57:10.498
He said, your mother must come home immediately.

00:57:10.558 --> 00:57:13.082
I will come back tonight."

00:57:13.142 --> 00:57:18.614
Meg said Joe, we must send the telegram to Marmy.

00:57:18.674 --> 00:57:23.415
Joe put on her coat and hat and she ran outside.

00:57:23.475 --> 00:57:26.416
Laurie was walking towards the house.

00:57:26.476 --> 00:57:29.167
He was holding a letter in his hand.

00:57:29.227 --> 00:57:32.338
He was very happy and excited.

00:57:32.398 --> 00:57:35.469
I have good news, he said.

00:57:35.529 --> 00:57:38.090
This letter is from John Brooke.

00:57:38.150 --> 00:57:40.938
Your father is getting better now.

00:57:40.998 --> 00:57:43.376
But what's wrong, Joe?

00:57:43.436 --> 00:57:45.406
Where are you going?

00:57:45.466 --> 00:57:50.250
I'm going to send a telegram to Marmy," replied Joe.

00:57:50.310 --> 00:57:53.032
Dr. Bang's visited Beth.

00:57:53.092 --> 00:57:55.714
She is very, very ill.

00:57:55.774 --> 00:57:58.427
Joe started to cry.

00:57:58.487 --> 00:58:01.600
Laurie held Joe's hand.

00:58:01.660 --> 00:58:07.404
Dear Joe, he said, grandfather and I will always help you.

00:58:07.464 --> 00:58:09.631
Please remember that.

00:58:09.691 --> 00:58:12.068
Yes, said Joe.

00:58:12.129 --> 00:58:14.230
You are our good friends.

00:58:14.290 --> 00:58:17.252
Thank you very much.

00:58:17.312 --> 00:58:21.956
I must tell you something, said Laurie.

00:58:22.016 --> 00:58:26.488
Last week, grandfather and I were talking about Beth.

00:58:26.548 --> 00:58:29.070
We were very worried about her.

00:58:29.130 --> 00:58:32.062
We sent a telegram to your mother.

00:58:32.122 --> 00:58:35.144
We told her about Beth's illness.

00:58:35.205 --> 00:58:39.074
Today, I received this letter from John Brooke.

00:58:39.134 --> 00:58:42.731
Your mother will be here early tomorrow morning.

00:58:42.791 --> 00:58:45.752
Then everything will be all right.

00:58:45.812 --> 00:58:48.174
Joe was happy again.

00:58:48.234 --> 00:58:50.214
She stopped crying.

00:58:50.274 --> 00:58:54.866
Laurie, she said, you're a wonderful friend.

00:58:54.926 --> 00:58:56.966
Thank you.

00:58:57.027 --> 00:59:00.048
Joe ran inside the house.

00:59:00.108 --> 00:59:02.499
She told Meg the good news.

00:59:02.559 --> 00:59:06.221
Meg was very happy too.

00:59:06.281 --> 00:59:10.244
The afternoon passed slowly.

00:59:10.304 --> 00:59:12.626
Beth lay in her bed.

00:59:12.687 --> 00:59:14.928
Her eyes were closed.

00:59:14.988 --> 00:59:17.911
She did not eat or speak.

00:59:17.972 --> 00:59:21.194
Sometimes she drank some water.

00:59:21.254 --> 00:59:24.236
Meghan Joe sat by her bed.

00:59:24.296 --> 00:59:27.770
The wind blew and the snow fell.

00:59:27.830 --> 00:59:30.762
At last night came.

00:59:30.822 --> 00:59:33.594
Meghan Joe watched Beth.

00:59:33.654 --> 00:59:39.605
They waited for Mrs. March, and they waited for Dr. Bangs.

00:59:39.666 --> 00:59:43.818
Old Mr. Lawrence and Laurie waited, too.

00:59:43.878 --> 00:59:46.860
They sat downstairs in the living room.

00:59:46.920 --> 00:59:49.411
They sat by the fire.

00:59:49.472 --> 00:59:52.324
The hours passed.

00:59:52.384 --> 00:59:56.686
At two o'clock in the morning, Joe went to the window.

00:59:56.746 --> 00:59:58.987
She looked out at the garden.

00:59:59.048 --> 01:00:02.603
There was thick snow everywhere.

01:00:02.663 --> 01:00:08.158
The world is sad and lonely tonight, she thought.

01:00:08.218 --> 01:00:10.728
Suddenly she heard a noise.

01:00:10.788 --> 01:00:12.389
She turned round.

01:00:12.449 --> 01:00:14.859
Meg was crying.

01:00:14.919 --> 01:00:18.330
Beth has died, thought Joe.

01:00:18.390 --> 01:00:22.781
Beth has died, and Meg cannot tell me.

01:00:22.841 --> 01:00:26.252
She went to the bed and looked down at Beth.

01:00:26.312 --> 01:00:28.132
Beth was quiet.

01:00:28.192 --> 01:00:30.852
Her eyes were closed.

01:00:30.912 --> 01:00:33.194
Then the door opened.

01:00:33.254 --> 01:00:36.138
And Dr. Bangs came into the room.

01:00:36.198 --> 01:00:40.682
Beth is dead, Joe said quietly.

01:00:40.742 --> 01:00:43.364
Dr. Bangs looked at Beth.

01:00:43.424 --> 01:00:45.375
He held her hands.

01:00:45.436 --> 01:00:47.797
Then he smiled.

01:00:47.858 --> 01:00:50.270
No, he said.

01:00:50.330 --> 01:00:52.411
Beth isn't dead.

01:00:52.472 --> 01:00:54.033
She's sleeping.

01:00:54.093 --> 01:00:56.245
She's going to be all right.

01:00:56.305 --> 01:00:59.171
There is no more danger.

01:00:59.231 --> 01:01:03.917
Meghan Cho put their arms around each other and they cried.

01:01:03.977 --> 01:01:07.949
They were very, very happy.

01:01:08.009 --> 01:01:11.510
Soon it was morning.

01:01:11.570 --> 01:01:16.563
The sisters heard the sound of a carriage in the street.

01:01:16.623 --> 01:01:25.618
Then Laurie called from the living room, girls, girls, your mother is here.

01:01:25.678 --> 01:01:36.340
Mrs. March had come home.

01:01:36.400 --> 01:01:53.804
Chapter 10 The Best Christmas Present Amy was unhappy at Aunt March's house.

01:01:53.864 --> 01:01:56.556
She wanted to see her family.

01:01:56.616 --> 01:01:59.279
Aunt March was an old lady.

01:01:59.340 --> 01:02:01.903
She did not like young girls.

01:02:01.963 --> 01:02:05.202
Sometimes she was angry with Amy.

01:02:05.263 --> 01:02:12.874
Every evening Amy had to read to Aunt March, but she did not like Aunt March's books.

01:02:12.934 --> 01:02:15.846
They were not very interesting.

01:02:15.906 --> 01:02:19.928
One evening Aunt March spoke to Amy.

01:02:19.988 --> 01:02:24.242
I have had a letter from your mother, she said.

01:02:24.302 --> 01:02:26.333
She has come home.

01:02:26.393 --> 01:02:29.755
She will take you home tomorrow.

01:02:29.816 --> 01:02:33.322
Amy was very happy.

01:02:33.382 --> 01:02:41.180
Soon the four sisters were together again, and every day Beth was stronger.

01:02:41.241 --> 01:02:45.513
One day a letter came from Washington.

01:02:45.573 --> 01:02:48.064
It was from John Brooke.

01:02:48.125 --> 01:02:50.826
Mrs. March read the letter.

01:02:50.886 --> 01:02:56.810
Girls, girls, I have wonderful news, she said.

01:02:56.870 --> 01:03:01.810
Mr. Brooke is going to bring Father home.

01:03:01.870 --> 01:03:05.780
It was a week before Christmas.

01:03:05.840 --> 01:03:09.772
The March sisters were very busy and excited.

01:03:09.832 --> 01:03:16.817
They made Christmas presents, and they cooked delicious food for Christmas day.

01:03:16.878 --> 01:03:21.190
In the evening, Joe spoke to her mother.

01:03:21.250 --> 01:03:26.294
Marme, she said, I must tell you something.

01:03:26.354 --> 01:03:29.486
John Brooke loves Meg.

01:03:29.547 --> 01:03:32.940
In the summer, Meg lost a glove.

01:03:33.000 --> 01:03:37.192
John Brooke found it, and he put it in his pocket.

01:03:37.252 --> 01:03:40.304
Isn't that terrible, Marme?

01:03:40.364 --> 01:03:42.825
Why is it terrible?

01:03:42.885 --> 01:03:44.766
asked Mrs. March.

01:03:44.826 --> 01:03:48.878
John Brooke will marry Meg, replied Joe.

01:03:48.938 --> 01:03:51.490
He'll take her away from us.

01:03:51.551 --> 01:03:55.362
Listen, Joe, said Mrs. March.

01:03:55.422 --> 01:03:58.624
John Brooke is a good young man.

01:03:58.684 --> 01:04:02.603
He was very kind and helpful in Washington.

01:04:02.663 --> 01:04:07.483
John Brooke must not marry Meg," Joe said.

01:04:07.543 --> 01:04:11.076
Meg must not marry a poor man.

01:04:11.136 --> 01:04:16.229
Money is not important, replied Mrs. March.

01:04:16.289 --> 01:04:18.901
John is good and kind.

01:04:18.961 --> 01:04:21.652
He loves Meg very much.

01:04:21.712 --> 01:04:23.984
But Meg is young.

01:04:24.044 --> 01:04:26.346
She is only seventeen.

01:04:26.406 --> 01:04:28.597
They must wait.

01:04:28.657 --> 01:04:33.578
Please don't be sad, Joe," Mrs. March said.

01:04:33.638 --> 01:04:36.819
One day you will leave this house, too.

01:04:36.879 --> 01:04:40.920
You will meet a good man and you will marry him.

01:04:40.980 --> 01:04:43.401
No, mother, cried Joe.

01:04:43.461 --> 01:04:45.672
I'll never marry anybody.

01:04:45.732 --> 01:04:49.402
I want to be a famous writer.

01:04:49.462 --> 01:04:54.184
At last it was Christmas Day.

01:04:54.244 --> 01:04:56.664
Everybody had some presents.

01:04:56.724 --> 01:04:59.174
Everybody was happy.

01:04:59.234 --> 01:05:05.065
In the afternoon, Laurie and old Mr. Lawrence came to the March's house.

01:05:05.125 --> 01:05:06.976
They brought presents.

01:05:07.036 --> 01:05:10.677
Everybody talked and everybody laughed.

01:05:10.737 --> 01:05:15.068
Then somebody knocked at the front door.

01:05:15.129 --> 01:05:18.190
Laurie went to the door.

01:05:18.250 --> 01:05:21.811
A moment later, he came back into the living room.

01:05:21.871 --> 01:05:24.302
He was very excited.

01:05:24.362 --> 01:05:29.818
Here is another Christmas present for the March family, he said.

01:05:29.878 --> 01:05:33.734
A tall man was standing behind Laurie.

01:05:33.794 --> 01:05:36.314
Everybody looked at the man.

01:05:36.374 --> 01:05:39.436
For a moment, they did not speak.

01:05:39.496 --> 01:05:45.288
Then the girls shouted together, Father!

01:05:45.348 --> 01:05:49.780
All the sisters ran to their father.

01:05:49.840 --> 01:05:52.211
They put their arms around him.

01:05:52.271 --> 01:05:55.512
Everybody was talking and crying.

01:05:55.572 --> 01:06:00.234
This is the best Christmas present, said Amy.

01:06:00.294 --> 01:06:03.364
Then another man came into the room.

01:06:03.424 --> 01:06:05.396
It was John Brooke.

01:06:05.456 --> 01:06:08.058
Meg ran towards him.

01:06:08.118 --> 01:06:12.402
I'm very happy to see you, John, she said.

01:06:12.462 --> 01:06:13.782
Thank you.

01:06:13.842 --> 01:06:17.185
You have brought Father home to us.

01:06:17.245 --> 01:06:21.298
Later, everybody ate Christmas dinner.

01:06:21.358 --> 01:06:24.770
Then the Lawrence's and John Brooke went home.

01:06:24.830 --> 01:06:27.972
The March family sat by the fire.

01:06:28.033 --> 01:06:32.824
Mr. March looked at the faces of his four happy daughters.

01:06:32.884 --> 01:06:39.676
My dears, he said, this year has been very long and difficult.

01:06:39.736 --> 01:06:42.467
You had to work very hard.

01:06:42.527 --> 01:06:45.538
I left home and you were girls.

01:06:45.598 --> 01:06:47.898
Now you have grown up.

01:06:47.958 --> 01:06:51.196
You are four fine women.

01:06:51.256 --> 01:06:55.575
Chapter 11 A Happy Ending The marches were together again.

01:06:55.635 --> 01:07:09.231
Every day, Mr. March and Beth were stronger.

01:07:09.291 --> 01:07:22.654
Laurie and old Mr. Lawrence often visited the marches.

01:07:22.714 --> 01:07:25.865
But John Brooke did not come with them.

01:07:25.925 --> 01:07:27.855
Meg was sad.

01:07:27.915 --> 01:07:31.276
She wanted to see John very much.

01:07:31.336 --> 01:07:34.817
I don't understand, she thought.

01:07:34.877 --> 01:07:38.178
Why doesn't John visit us?

01:07:38.238 --> 01:07:42.739
One afternoon, Meg and Joe were talking.

01:07:42.799 --> 01:07:46.390
Joe saw an umbrella by the front door.

01:07:46.450 --> 01:07:48.911
Who's umbrella is that?"

01:07:48.971 --> 01:07:50.172
she asked.

01:07:50.232 --> 01:07:52.934
I've never seen it before.

01:07:52.995 --> 01:07:57.188
It's John Brooke's umbrella, replied Meg.

01:07:57.248 --> 01:08:00.110
He left it here on Christmas Day.

01:08:00.170 --> 01:08:02.622
He has forgotten it.

01:08:02.682 --> 01:08:05.634
Meg, said Joe.

01:08:05.694 --> 01:08:08.226
Do you like John Brooke?

01:08:08.286 --> 01:08:10.538
Do you love him?

01:08:10.598 --> 01:08:13.409
Are you going to marry him?

01:08:13.470 --> 01:08:16.786
No, no, Meg said.

01:08:16.846 --> 01:08:19.551
I'm too young for marriage.

01:08:19.610 --> 01:08:23.402
Please don't ask me these questions, Joe.

01:08:23.461 --> 01:08:27.002
Then you don't love him, said Joe.

01:08:27.062 --> 01:08:31.354
Oh, I don't know, said Meg.

01:08:31.413 --> 01:08:33.954
Joe looked out of the window.

01:08:34.014 --> 01:08:38.105
Meg, John Brooke is outside now, she said.

01:08:38.165 --> 01:08:40.316
He is coming to the front door.

01:08:40.376 --> 01:08:42.166
You don't love him, Meg.

01:08:42.226 --> 01:08:43.807
He must go away.

01:08:43.867 --> 01:08:45.818
Please tell him.

01:08:45.878 --> 01:08:48.300
Meg ran to the stairs.

01:08:48.360 --> 01:08:52.982
She wanted to hide in her bedroom, but it was too late.

01:08:53.042 --> 01:08:55.902
John Brooke came into the house.

01:08:55.962 --> 01:08:57.803
Good afternoon.

01:08:57.863 --> 01:09:01.505
John said, do you have my umbrella?

01:09:01.565 --> 01:09:03.166
I left it here.

01:09:03.226 --> 01:09:04.536
He smiled.

01:09:04.596 --> 01:09:08.127
Then he said, how is your father?

01:09:08.187 --> 01:09:11.498
He's very well, thank you, said Joe.

01:09:11.558 --> 01:09:13.486
We'll bring him.

01:09:13.546 --> 01:09:17.626
Joe went upstairs, and Meg started to follow.

01:09:17.685 --> 01:09:20.188
But John Brooks stopped her.

01:09:20.248 --> 01:09:22.509
Please don't go, Meg.

01:09:22.569 --> 01:09:26.832
He said, I must say something to you.

01:09:26.891 --> 01:09:29.384
Oh, said Meg.

01:09:29.444 --> 01:09:32.346
Let's talk in the living room.

01:09:32.406 --> 01:09:35.568
John and Meg went into the living room.

01:09:35.628 --> 01:09:39.741
Meg sat down, and John Brooks sat beside her.

01:09:39.801 --> 01:09:42.936
He held her hand.

01:09:42.996 --> 01:09:48.253
Dearest Meg, he said, I love you.

01:09:48.273 --> 01:09:52.216
I am poor, but I can work hard.

01:09:52.276 --> 01:09:55.068
I can make a good home for you.

01:09:55.128 --> 01:09:59.542
Please Meg, will you be my wife?

01:09:59.602 --> 01:10:03.204
At first Meg did not speak.

01:10:03.264 --> 01:10:07.738
Then she said, I don't know John.

01:10:07.798 --> 01:10:10.850
Please Meg, said John Brooke.

01:10:10.910 --> 01:10:13.122
Will you marry me?

01:10:13.182 --> 01:10:18.305
Suddenly the door opened and Aunt March came into the room.

01:10:18.365 --> 01:10:21.447
Meghan John were very surprised.

01:10:21.507 --> 01:10:24.259
Aunt March was surprised, too.

01:10:24.319 --> 01:10:26.570
Good afternoon, Meg.

01:10:26.630 --> 01:10:29.503
She said, where is your father?

01:10:29.562 --> 01:10:31.894
Then she looked at John Brooke.

01:10:31.954 --> 01:10:34.066
Who is this young man?

01:10:34.086 --> 01:10:39.310
Aunt March, this is John Brooke, Meg said.

01:10:39.370 --> 01:10:41.938
John is father's friend.

01:10:41.997 --> 01:10:45.525
John Brooke, said Aunt March.

01:10:45.585 --> 01:10:47.986
Why are you here, young man?

01:10:48.046 --> 01:10:50.458
What are you talking about?

01:10:50.518 --> 01:10:54.119
Aunt March, said Meg quietly.

01:10:54.179 --> 01:10:57.590
John Brooke wants to marry me.

01:10:57.650 --> 01:11:01.282
Aunt March looked angrily at John Brooke.

01:11:01.342 --> 01:11:07.534
Then she said, young man, Mrs. March has spoken about you.

01:11:07.594 --> 01:11:08.935
You are poor.

01:11:08.995 --> 01:11:10.546
You have no money.

01:11:10.606 --> 01:11:13.976
Meg must marry a man with money.

01:11:14.036 --> 01:11:16.668
Meg was very angry.

01:11:16.728 --> 01:11:19.270
And March, she said.

01:11:19.330 --> 01:11:24.862
John is poor, but he is a good man, and I love him.

01:11:24.922 --> 01:11:29.195
John Brooke smiled, and his eyes were bright.

01:11:29.255 --> 01:11:32.917
Thank you, dearest Meg, he said.

01:11:32.977 --> 01:11:34.538
Do you love me?

01:11:34.598 --> 01:11:36.509
Will you marry me?

01:11:36.569 --> 01:11:40.127
Yes, I will, said Meg.

01:11:40.187 --> 01:11:45.635
Meg said Aunt March, you are a very foolish girl.

01:11:45.695 --> 01:11:48.816
You will never get any money from me.

01:11:48.876 --> 01:11:50.367
Goodbye."

01:11:50.427 --> 01:11:54.369
She turned round and went quickly out of the room.

01:11:54.428 --> 01:11:58.980
Meghan John told the March family their good news.

01:11:59.040 --> 01:12:03.442
It's wonderful news, said Mr. and Mrs. March.

01:12:03.502 --> 01:12:05.494
Congratulations.

01:12:05.554 --> 01:12:10.396
Congratulations, said Amy and Beth together.

01:12:10.456 --> 01:12:13.779
Joe said nothing.

01:12:13.839 --> 01:12:18.131
She was not happy.

01:12:18.191 --> 01:12:24.184
Later, Laurie and Mr. Lawrence came to the house.

01:12:24.244 --> 01:12:30.267
They congratulated Meg and John, but Laurie looked at Joe's face.

01:12:30.327 --> 01:12:32.488
What's wrong, Joe?

01:12:32.548 --> 01:12:33.909
asked Laurie.

01:12:33.969 --> 01:12:35.770
Aren't you happy?

01:12:35.830 --> 01:12:38.252
No, said Joe.

01:12:38.312 --> 01:12:42.134
Meg is my dear sister and my dear friend.

01:12:42.195 --> 01:12:45.516
Now John Brooke will take her away.

01:12:45.576 --> 01:12:48.188
Joe, said Laurie.

01:12:48.248 --> 01:12:49.979
You love Meg.

01:12:50.040 --> 01:12:51.931
She is your sister.

01:12:51.991 --> 01:12:54.512
But John loves her too.

01:12:54.572 --> 01:12:57.334
Meg will be happy with John.

01:12:57.394 --> 01:13:01.198
And Joe, I'll always be your friend.

01:13:01.258 --> 01:13:04.009
That's true, said Joe.

01:13:04.069 --> 01:13:06.512
Thank you Laurie.

01:13:06.572 --> 01:13:09.716
Joe looked around the room.

01:13:09.776 --> 01:13:11.966
She looked at her family.

01:13:12.026 --> 01:13:15.387
Mr. and Mrs. March were talking together.

01:13:15.447 --> 01:13:19.108
Amy was sitting on the floor near Meghan John.

01:13:19.168 --> 01:13:22.680
Beth was talking to old Mr. Lawrence.

01:13:22.740 --> 01:13:26.160
Suddenly Joe was not sad anymore.

01:13:26.220 --> 01:13:28.311
She turned to Laurie.

01:13:28.371 --> 01:13:31.972
You are right, Laurie, she said.

01:13:32.032 --> 01:13:35.348
One day, Meg will marry John.

01:13:35.408 --> 01:13:38.274
But she will always be my sister.

01:13:38.334 --> 01:13:41.205
We will always love each other.

01:13:41.265 --> 01:13:45.066
That's right, Joe, said Laurie.

01:13:45.126 --> 01:13:47.707
Joe went over to Meg.

01:13:47.767 --> 01:13:51.638
She held Meg's hands and she kissed her face.

01:13:51.698 --> 01:13:56.470
Congratulations, dearest Meg, she said.

01:13:56.530 --> 01:13:59.131
I am very happy for you.

01:13:59.191 --> 01:14:02.052
And congratulations, John.

01:14:02.112 --> 01:14:04.624
You are our brother now.

01:14:04.684 --> 01:14:12.782
Welcome to our family.

01:14:12.842 --> 01:14:26.268
Little Women was read by Liza Ross and the recording was produced by James Richardson at Studio AVP London.

